    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d518">

                <pb facs="0619" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/986</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 9, 8 a. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>If discharge of innocent cargo necessary to get at prize cargo expenses of
                    warehousing, reshipment and dues must be paid by <pb facs="0620" n="362"
                        xml:id="pg362"/> ship and if not recoverable from ship then <hi
                        rendition="#italic">pro rata</hi> from cargo owners. April 1 I appealed to
                    prize court for ruling which would free ship and innocent cargo from all dues
                    and expenses arising from Government’s orders. President replies declining to
                    instruct Admiralty marshal except in consequence of proceedings in form of
                    judgment. Therefore unless representations are made to Government, all detained
                    ships will be required themselves to pay costs resulting exclusively from orders
                    of Admiralty.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
